# @epistemologic/liquid_extraction — sibling family-root at the
# logical altitude of the doc-code seam. Landed per Seam Phase D
# pre-review at `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md`
# §1 (Interpretation B RATIFIED as canonical: narrative ABOVE `---`;
# `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW) and Seam Phase D
# ratification at `820a451` on TICK 1 `shards/docblock.mirror` family-root
# (`5c0f5ba`). This shard follows TICK 1 as the sibling family-root at
# the logical altitude of the doc-claim operator per Mara spec §3
# four-altitude structure.
#
# === Sibling relationship to @docblock ===
#
# @docblock (family-root landed TICK 1 at `5c0f5ba`) declares the
# doc-claim carrier surface: `doc_claim`, `claim_kind`, `docblock`,
# `audit_boundary`, `docblock_verdict`, plus the routing actions
# (`extract_claims`, `project`, `audit_docblock`, `docblock_well_audited`).
# @epistemologic/liquid_extraction is the SIBLING family-root at the
# next altitude in Mara §3: it lowers doc-claim narrative to liquid
# predicates the substrate's `@projection.preview` verdict machinery
# can decide. Sibling — not parent, not child — because the two
# family-roots operate at COUPLED altitudes on the same operator
# (per recognition #59 the doc-claim operator is altitude-portable);
# one names the carrier; the other names the extraction.
#
# The `in @docblock` import below the seam grounds the sibling
# relationship at the substrate level: this shard's `extractor_input`
# specializes @docblock's `doc_claim`. Bilateral discipline per
# recognition #53 sixth-instance (see below) closes the two-way
# coupling: @docblock's `extract_claims` action returns claims;
# @epistemologic/liquid_extraction's `extract_predicate` lifts each
# claim to a liquid predicate.
#
# === Logical altitude per Mara §3 four-altitude structure ===
#
# Mara's compiler-fit doc §3 names four altitudes on the same
# doc-claim operator, all altitude-portable per recognition #59:
#
# - linguistic — @epistemologic/property/docblock_{grounded,coherent,
#   no_extraction_pattern} audit docblock language before it enters
#   the type system. Landing in follow-up ticks; three property/
#   fracture bilateral pairs.
# - logical — THIS SHARD. @epistemologic/liquid_extraction lowers
#   doc claims to liquid predicates per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008
#   + Vazou et al 2014. The substrate's `@projection.preview` verdict
#   IS the decidable fragment; the extractor produces its input.
#   Extractor body forward-promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`.
# - temporal — the projection surface at `63bdecc` projects doc
#   claims forward k=3 substrate ticks as typed carriers landed
#   back in the doc's own observation side (below `---`).
# - publishable — docblock claims across `shards/` aggregate into
#   case-study crystals at systemic.engineering.
#
# The logical altitude sits BETWEEN linguistic (audit surface at
# language altitude) and temporal (projection surface at recognition-
# candidate altitude). It is the altitude at which linguistic material
# becomes formally decidable — the substrate's liquid-refinement
# fragment per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala + Vazou. Named "logical" per
# Mara §3 because the operator here is proof-theoretic (predicates
# on data) as opposed to linguistic (narrative parse) or temporal
# (forward-projection).
#
# === Property/fracture bilateral pattern (#53 sixth-instance) ===
#
# Per recognition #53 the substrate has a bilateral pattern:
# declarative property at `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` +
# operational fracture body at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`,
# bridged by the kintsugi loop. Fifth instance landed at
# `@kintsugi/surface` + `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.
# ashby_variety_match` (2026-07-03 `e910dd6`). The SIXTH FAMILY at
# the doc-claim altitude is grounded at TICK 1's @docblock landing;
# each of the three property/fracture pairs (grounded, coherent,
# no_extraction_pattern) is a #53-shaped bilateral instance landing
# in follow-up ticks per Mara spec §3-§8.
#
# This shard's `liquid_extraction_sound` bilateral predicate carries
# the operational half of the extractor's discipline: the extractor
# is sound when its lowered predicate soundly reflects the doc
# claim's substrate-observable content. Fracture-side body forward-
# promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` at species-depth 1
# under @epistemologic per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace.
# The depth mirrors the property-family bilateral pattern the
# substrate uses at `@epistemologic/property/*` and
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/*`: extraction is an epistemologic
# discipline (the substrate is checking what it can know about a
# doc claim's predicate content), not a doc-claim carrier
# (that lives at @docblock).
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# The operator must audit its own audit at depth=3 per `63bdecc` §6.
# This shard's own docblock must survive `audit_docblock(this_docblock,
# depth=3)` and `liquid_extraction_sound(extract_claims(this_docblock),
# verdict)` per the sibling coupling. At this tick, the extractor's
# body is forward-promised, so the self-audit verdict at logical
# altitude is `unextractable` — the honest answer given no extractor
# is landed. Promotion of `liquid_extraction_sound` to a decidable
# verdict awaits the extractor body and property/fracture bilateral
# trio.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @docblock

prism @epistemologic/liquid_extraction {
  focus liquid_extraction
  project liquid_extraction
  split liquid_extraction
  shift liquid_extraction
  settle liquid_extraction
}

# === extractor_input — one doc_claim as extraction input (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: the extractor input is exactly a @docblock-side
# `doc_claim`. Newtyped per `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]`; the alias
# to `doc_claim` names the sibling coupling at the type level.
type extractor_input = doc_claim

# === predicate_shape — extractor output carrier (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: the extractor's output is a `splinter(@epistemo-
# logic/property/ast)` fragment carried at ref shape per the
# substrate's content-addressing discipline. Newtyped per
# `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]` so the extraction output is not
# confused with any other ref-shape at this altitude.
type predicate_shape = ref

# === extraction_verdict — four variants (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: the four-verdict output specializes the
# `@projection.preview` verdict machinery to the liquid-extraction
# altitude. `satisfiable` — extractor lowered the claim to a liquid
# predicate the substrate can decide; `unsatisfiable` — lowered but
# the predicate is provably false against the substrate below;
# `partial` — extractor lowered part of the claim (composite
# narrative with mixed groundable + non-groundable clauses);
# `unextractable` — extractor could not lower the claim at all
# (natural language beyond the liquid fragment; no predicate shape
# recoverable). Grounds Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008 decidability
# fragment + Vazou et al 2014 refinement discipline at doc-claim
# altitude.
type extraction_verdict =
  | satisfiable
  | unsatisfiable
  | partial
  | unextractable

# === extract_predicate — extractor_input → ref (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: lowers a doc_claim to a `splinter(@epistemologic/
# property/ast)` fragment carrying the liquid predicate. Output is
# a ref carrying the splinter(ast) discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`. Body forward-promised
# per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`; discharge via splinter(ast)
# at the property altitude when the extractor lands.
extract_predicate(i: extractor_input) -> ref { \ }

# === liquid_extraction_sound — bilateral predicate (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2 the #53-family bilateral: the extractor is sound
# when its lowered predicate soundly reflects the doc claim's
# substrate-observable content. Carries the declarative-side
# property; the operational-side fracture body lands with the
# property/fracture bilateral pairs in follow-up ticks per Mara
# spec §3-§8. Body forward-promised — discharge via
# `splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast)` against the extractor's
# output AST fragment when the extractor body lands.
liquid_extraction_sound(i: extractor_input, v: extraction_verdict) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
out extractor_input
out predicate_shape
out extraction_verdict
out extract_predicate
out liquid_extraction_sound
